{#
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  AN ORGANISATION'S OWN PAGE — THE READER THAT DID NOT EXIST
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  `OrgBrand` shipped complete on every side except a renderer. There was a validated
  writer, an accent refused for failing contrast against white with the ratio in the
  message, an uploader, a route, and `css()` to turn the whole document into custom
  properties — and `css()` had no caller, `DonationController` never mentioned the
  service, and the organisation's own dashboard template contained the word "brand"
  zero times. No form in, no page out, while the migration's docblock described the
  feature as shipped. This file and the editor on the dashboard are the two halves of
  the fix; neither is worth anything alone.

  ── WHAT IS RENDERED, AND ON WHAT CONDITION ─────────────────────────────────

  A block appears when it is SWITCHED ON *and* has content. Both, deliberately: a bare
  "Questions donors ask you" heading over nothing reads as a page somebody abandoned
  halfway, which on a donation page costs the organisation real money. So the section
  flag alone is not enough to publish a heading.

  ── EVERYTHING HERE IS UNTRUSTED ────────────────────────────────────────────

  Every string below was typed by a partner organisation. Twig's autoescaping is what
  makes that safe, so nothing here may gain `|raw`. The two places that could not rely
  on escaping alone are handled in the service instead: a link's URL is re-validated on
  every read by `OrgBrand::url()`, and a video is stored as a provider plus an id and
  never as a URL, so `v.embed` below is built by `OrgBrand::embedUrl()` from our own
  constant and a pattern-matched id. Nothing an organisation typed ever reaches an
  `src`.

  The accent values in the `style` attribute are safe for the same kind of reason
  rather than by escaping: `normaliseHex()` returns either an empty string or `#` and
  six hex digits, and the wash is assembled with `%d` from integers. A `style`
  attribute is HTML-escaped by Twig, not CSS-escaped, so a value that could carry a
  brace or a semicolon would matter here — none of these can.

  ── VIDEO IS CLICK-TO-LOAD, AND THAT IS A LEGAL REQUIREMENT ─────────────────

  An iframe that loads on page view sends the visitor's IP address to YouTube or Vimeo
  and lets them set storage, before the visitor has done anything at all. Under the
  GDPR's joint-controller line and Nigeria's NDPA 2023 that needs a lawful basis, and
  "the page happened to contain a video" is not one. `youtube-nocookie.com` narrows the
  cookie question and does not touch the transmission.

  So nothing reaches either provider until somebody presses play, the button says which
  provider it will contact before they do, and there is a plain link out for anybody
  whose browser refuses the frame. The handler is in donate.twig's nonce'd script
  block. This is also why the accent is on the facade and not on a poster image we
  would have to fetch from the provider to display.
#}

{% if org and brand %}
<div class="ob"
     style="--ob-accent:{{ brand_css.accent }};--ob-accent-dark:{{ brand_css.accent_dark }};--ob-accent-wash:{{ brand_css.accent_wash }}">

  {# ── THE STORY ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Paragraphs come from `OrgBrand::paragraphs()` rather than a filter here, so one
     definition of "a paragraph" serves this page and every later surface. The story
     used to arrive with every newline collapsed, so five paragraphs about somebody's
     work rendered as one block that read like a notice. #}
  {% if brand.sections.story and story_paragraphs is not empty %}
    <section class="dn-sec ob-sec">
      <span class="dn-kick">Our story</span>
      <h2 class="dn-h2">About {{ org.name }}</h2>
      <div class="ob-prose">
        {% for p in story_paragraphs %}<p>{{ p }}</p>{% endfor %}
      </div>
    </section>
  {% endif %}

  {# ── THE FIGURES ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     A figure is the organisation's own claim and is presented as one — the kicker says
     "in their words", because this platform verifies a registration and a settlement
     account and does not audit an impact number. Printing an unverified figure in the
     same voice as a verified one is how a page stops being evidence of anything. #}
  {% if brand.sections.impact and brand.blocks.impact is not empty %}
    <section class="dn-sec ob-sec">
      <span class="dn-kick">The work, in their words</span>
      <h2 class="dn-h2">What {{ org.name }} has done</h2>
      <div class="ob-figs">
        {% for row in brand.blocks.impact %}
          <div class="ob-fig">
            <div class="ob-fig__n">{{ row.figure }}</div>
            <div class="ob-fig__l">{{ row.label }}</div>
          </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </section>
  {% endif %}

  {# ── WHAT A GIFT BUYS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     A ladder, and the highest-earning block on a donation page: "₦25,000" means
     nothing and "₦25,000 sends one student for a term" means something.

     DISPLAY ONLY, and it says so nowhere on the page because a reader does not need to
     know — but the next person editing this does. These rows do not preset the amount
     field. Wiring them to it is worth doing and is a change to the form's own state, so
     it is deliberately not smuggled in here: a row that looks pressable and does
     nothing is worse than a row that is plainly a list. #}
  {% if brand.sections.asks and brand.blocks.asks is not empty %}
    <section class="dn-sec ob-sec">
      <span class="dn-kick">What a gift buys</span>
      <h2 class="dn-h2">Where your money goes</h2>
      <ul class="ob-asks">
        {% for row in brand.blocks.asks %}
          <li><span class="ob-asks__a">{{ row.amount }}</span>
              <span class="ob-asks__b">{{ row.buys }}</span></li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </section>
  {% endif %}

  {# ── VIDEO ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     See the note at the top of this file for why this is a facade and not an iframe. #}
  {% if brand.sections.video and brand.videos is not empty %}
    <section class="dn-sec ob-sec">
      <span class="dn-kick">Watch</span>
      <h2 class="dn-h2">{{ org.name }} on film</h2>
      <div class="ob-vids">
        {% for v in brand.videos %}
          {% set provider = v.provider == 'vimeo' ? 'Vimeo' : 'YouTube' %}
          <figure class="ob-vid" data-ob-video data-ob-src="{{ v.embed }}"
                  data-ob-name="{{ v.title ?: (org.name ~ ' — video') }}">
            <button type="button" class="ob-vid__play" data-ob-play
                    aria-label="Play {{ v.title ?: 'the video' }} — loads from {{ provider }}">
              <span class="ob-vid__icon" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="currentColor"
                     focusable="false"><path d="M8 5v14l11-7z"/></svg>
              </span>
              <span class="ob-vid__meta">
                {% if v.title %}<span class="ob-vid__t">{{ v.title }}</span>{% endif %}
                {# Named BEFORE the press, not after it. A visitor deciding whether to
                   contact a third party is owed the name of the third party. #}
                <span class="ob-vid__p">Loads from {{ provider }} when you press play</span>
              </span>
            </button>
            {# For a browser that refuses the frame — an extension, a strict policy, a
               provider outage. The alternative is a dead rectangle, which is the shape of
               fault this codebase keeps paying for: no error, nothing to grep, the
               feature simply not there. #}
            <figcaption class="ob-vid__alt">
              <a href="{{ v.watch }}" target="_blank"
                 rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow ugc">Watch on {{ provider }}</a>
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </section>
  {% endif %}

  {# ── PHOTOGRAPHS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Paths are re-checked by `OrgBrand::safePath()` on every read, which refuses
     anything that is not a relative path beneath `uploads/`. So this cannot address a
     file outside it however the row was written. #}
  {% if brand.sections.gallery and brand.gallery is not empty %}
    <section class="dn-sec ob-sec">
      <span class="dn-kick">The work</span>
      <h2 class="dn-h2">Photographs</h2>
      <div class="ob-shots">
        {% for path in brand.gallery %}
          <img src="{{ asset('/' ~ path) }}" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </section>
  {% endif %}

  {# ── WHAT PEOPLE SAY ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────#}
  {% if brand.sections.quotes and brand.blocks.quotes is not empty %}
    <section class="dn-sec ob-sec">
      <span class="dn-kick">In their words</span>
      <h2 class="dn-h2">What people say</h2>
      <div class="ob-quotes">
        {% for row in brand.blocks.quotes %}
          <blockquote class="ob-quote">
            <p>{{ row.text }}</p>
            <cite>{{ row.who }}</cite>
          </blockquote>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </section>
  {% endif %}

  {# ── WHO RUNS IT ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Names and roles only, no photographs. A donor asking "who are these people" is
     answered by a name they can search; a headshot is the expensive half and the half
     that goes stale. Kept text-only rather than adding a second upload surface. #}
  {% if brand.sections.team and brand.blocks.team is not empty %}
    <section class="dn-sec ob-sec">
      <span class="dn-kick">The people</span>
      <h2 class="dn-h2">Who runs {{ org.name }}</h2>
      <ul class="ob-people">
        {% for row in brand.blocks.team %}
          <li><span class="ob-people__n">{{ row.name }}</span>
              <span class="ob-people__r">{{ row.role }}</span></li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </section>
  {% endif %}

  {# ── HOW THEY GOT HERE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     `when` is free text, not a date column, and deliberately: an organisation writing
     "2019", "March 2021" and "the first term of 2023" is describing their own history
     at the precision they actually have it, and a date picker would force them to
     invent a day. Nothing sorts on it — the order is the order they typed. #}
  {% if brand.sections.milestones and brand.blocks.milestones is not empty %}
    <section class="dn-sec ob-sec">
      <span class="dn-kick">How we got here</span>
      <h2 class="dn-h2">A short history</h2>
      <ol class="ob-track">
        {% for row in brand.blocks.milestones %}
          <li><span class="ob-track__w">{{ row.when }}</span>
              <span class="ob-track__d">{{ row.what }}</span></li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ol>
    </section>
  {% endif %}

  {# ── WHO THEY WORK WITH ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Names, not logos. A wall of logos an organisation uploaded is a wall of trademarks
     this platform would be republishing on their word, and the permission for that is
     between them and the trademark holder. A name and a sentence carries the same
     information and makes no claim we cannot stand behind. #}
  {% if brand.sections.partners and brand.blocks.partners is not empty %}
    <section class="dn-sec ob-sec">
      <span class="dn-kick">Together with</span>
      <h2 class="dn-h2">Who {{ org.name }} works with</h2>
      <ul class="ob-with">
        {% for row in brand.blocks.partners %}
          <li><span class="ob-with__n">{{ row.name }}</span>
              <span class="ob-with__d">{{ row.note }}</span></li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </section>
  {% endif %}

  {# ── QUESTIONS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     `<details>` rather than a scripted accordion: it is keyboard-operable and
     screen-reader-correct with no JavaScript, it prints open, and it is findable by the
     browser's own in-page search in every current engine. A scripted accordion is a
     worse version of this with a bug in it. #}
  {% if brand.sections.faq and brand.blocks.faq is not empty %}
    <section class="dn-sec ob-sec">
      <span class="dn-kick">Questions</span>
      <h2 class="dn-h2">What donors ask {{ org.name }}</h2>
      <div class="ob-faq">
        {% for row in brand.blocks.faq %}
          <details class="ob-faq__i">
            <summary>{{ row.q }}</summary>
            <div class="ob-faq__a">{{ row.a }}</div>
          </details>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </section>
  {% endif %}

  {# ── LINKS OUT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     `nofollow ugc` because these are links a partner typed and this platform does not
     vouch for them or pass it ranking; `noopener noreferrer` because a new tab that can
     reach back into this one is a tab that can rewrite the donation form. The host is
     printed beside the label so a reader knows where a press will take them before they
     make it — on a page asking for money, that is information they are owed. #}
  {% if brand.sections.links and brand.links is not empty %}
    <section class="dn-sec ob-sec">
      <span class="dn-kick">Read more</span>
      <h2 class="dn-h2">Reports, press and elsewhere</h2>
      <ul class="ob-links">
        {% for l in brand.links %}
          <li>
            <a href="{{ l.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow ugc">
              <span class="ob-links__l">{{ l.label }}</span>
              <span class="ob-links__h">{{ l.host }}<span aria-hidden="true"> ↗</span></span>
              <span class="ob-sr">opens in a new tab</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </section>
  {% endif %}

  {# ── HOW TO REACH THEM ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────#}
  {# Only `brand.website`, which they typed into a field labelled as public. NOT
     `org.contact_email`: that is the address given to verify their CAC registration, and
     publishing a compliance contact because it happens to be on the row is the kind of
     disclosure nobody notices until it is on a spam list. If an organisation wants a
     public address they can add one as a link. #}
  {% if brand.sections.contact and brand.website %}
    <section class="dn-sec ob-sec">
      <span class="dn-kick">Get in touch</span>
      <h2 class="dn-h2">Contact {{ org.name }}</h2>
      <ul class="ob-links ob-links--plain">
        {% if brand.website %}
          <li><a href="{{ brand.website }}" target="_blank"
                 rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow ugc">
            <span class="ob-links__l">Their website</span>
            <span class="ob-links__h">{{ brand.website|replace({'https://': '', 'http://': ''}) }}<span aria-hidden="true"> ↗</span></span>
          </a></li>
        {% endif %}
      </ul>
    </section>
  {% endif %}

  {# ══ AND THE PLATFORM UNDERNEATH IT ═══════════════════════════════════════
     Africa GATES provides this page, the checkout, the settlement into the
     organisation's own account, the receipting and the refund path, and takes no cut of
     any gift. Something has to pay for that, and the honest place to say so is the page
     the money moves through.

     BELOW the organisation's ask and never beside it. A charity's donation page with the
     platform's hand out next to theirs converts worse for the charity — the one thing
     this platform exists to be good at — and reads to a donor as two organisations
     arguing over one gift. So: a credit, one sentence of what that buys, and a quiet
     route for somebody who wants to back the awards themselves. No amount field, nothing
     preselected, and the organisation cannot switch it off. See OrgBrand::GATES_CREDIT. #}
  <section class="ob-gates">
    <p class="ob-gates__c">{{ gates_credit }}</p>
    <p class="ob-gates__b">{{ org.name }} keeps every naira of your gift — this platform
      takes no cut, charges them nothing, and settles straight into their own account.
      Africa GATES is a project of Afrovanguard, a registered non-profit, and it runs on
      optional support rather than on a fee.</p>
    {# `/philosophy` and `/donate` are both registered; `/giving` is NOT built yet and a
       credit line pointing at a 404 is worse than no credit at all. When /giving lands,
       this is the line that moves. #}
    <p class="ob-gates__l">
      <a href="/philosophy">What Africa GATES is</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
      <a href="/giving">Support the awards programme</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
{% endif %}
